  "body": "### What is the issue with the WebHID Standard?\n\nThe [`HIDCollectionInfo` dictionary](https://hid.spec.whatwg.org/#hidcollectioninfo-dictionary) has a member `sequence<HIDCollectionInfo> children;`. However, the [WebIDL spec states that for dictionaries](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-dictionary):\n\n> The type of a dictionary member must not include the dictionary it appears on. A type includes a dictionary D if at least one of the following is true:\n> - ...\n> - the type is a dictionary, one of whose members or inherited members has a type that includes D\n\nSo `HIDCollectionInfo` having a member of type `sequence<HIDCollectionInfo>` seems to be forbidden.\n\nI don't have a great idea for what to do about this, since it seems like HID requires this recursive type. Maybe we could change the WebIDL spec? Or at least put a note in the WebHID spec about this?",
